      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do you need this method? There are only two scenarios for legacy PIN pairing:\n\n1/ One of the two devices has a fixed PIN (hardcoded and provided as part of the device user guide) and the user has to type this PIN on the other devices. Which can be done using: `PairingEvent(method\u003dpin_code)` -\u003e `PairingEventAnswer(pin\u003d\u003cfixed PIN\u003e)`.\n\n2/ One device asks the user to enter a PIN code first, and then the second device asks the user to enter the same PIN code. Which can be done using: `PairingEvent(method\u003dpin_code)` -\u003e `PairingEventAnswer(pin\u003d\u003cprovided PIN\u003e)` on device 1 and then `PairingEvent(method\u003dpin_code)` -\u003e `PairingEventAnswer(pin\u003d\u003cprovided PIN\u003e) on device 2.\n\nThe reason why passkey entry is different is because 1/ does not exist but instead one of devices can automatically generate the passkey and show it to the user (`passkey_entry_notification`) and then the other device must entry the generated passkey.",
